    Five auditors (codex + xhigh + three Agents on disjoint areas) swept the whole
    repo, upstream code included. Worst: the optional Android document provider
    allowed path traversal out of its roots while serving a data dir that holds
    plaintext SESSDATA/access_key; enabling the proxy silently disabled TLS
    verification for all API traffic; anonymous requests still carried the
    account's csrf; error toasts printed access_key in the URL.
    
    Batch A (security/privacy/network/storage/platform/CI): provider traversal and
    subtree checks, proxy TLS, WebView mixed content and cookie lifecycle (incl.
    Linux WebKitGTK), csrf scrubbing, SponsorBlock server validation, cookie login
    parsing, WBI key caching, toast redaction, cross-origin redirect scrubbing
    (headers, query and body), note-page cookie scope, settings import validation,
    live socket reconnect, image save, download-path switch, crash log location,
    stream-mismatch resume, WebDAV backup/restore safety, CI signing guard,
    workflow permissions/SHA pinning, Windows/Linux launch-argument handling.
    
    Batch B (playback/danmaku/UI): danmaku weight filter, live danmaku tap crash,
    segment retry backoff, offline player no longer exposes account actions,
    danmaku speed on fullscreen, super-resolution state, pause heartbeat, mute
    sync, blacklist truncation, list refresh/load-more race, incognito gating of
    account-only menu items, local favorite removal, and ~20 smaller UI defects.
    
    User decisions this pass: expired accounts are marked, not deleted; login-only
    items hidden without an account; anti-fraud app's signing certificate verified
    before cookies are sent; retries limited to GET/HEAD; imports snapshot first;
    the comment check binds the account explicitly; exports ask before including
    credentials.
    
    Discovered via codex-audit on the whole codebase (96 findings, 63 fix groups,
    9 route picks). Verified on devices: OnePlus retest of the SAF local player,
    Mac sandbox probe (pass3-D7 confirmed), official anti-fraud APK fingerprint.
    
    Codex re-review verdict: ROUND-OK (69/70 resolved, A11 fixed in a follow-up).
    See audit-logs/pass-3.merged.jsonl for the full round-trip transcript.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

